---
// Why one blocking endpoint looks like a dead instance. 9.85 s is the
// /health latency in the /async-blocking capture next to the earlier figure.
const W = 900, H = 290;
const steps = [
  { en: ['one endpoint', 'blocks the loop'], vi: ['một endpoint', 'chặn loop'], red: true },
  { en: ['/health waits', 'behind it: 9.85 s'], vi: ['/health xếp sau nó', '9.85 s'], red: true },
  { en: ['the check', 'times out'], vi: ['health check', 'bị timeout'], red: false },
  { en: ['instance', 'declared dead'], vi: ['instance bị', 'coi là chết'], red: false },
];
---
<figure class="bep6i">
  <div class="bep6i-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Four steps: one endpoint blocks the event loop, the health check waits behind it for 9.85 seconds, the load balancer's check times out, and the instance is declared dead. The bug is in one endpoint but the whole process takes the blame.">
    {steps.map((s, i) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={30 + i * 220} y="50" width="180" height="84" rx="8" class={s.red ? 'bad' : 'box'} />
        <text x={120 + i * 220} y="86" text-anchor="middle" class={s.red ? 'vr' : 'v'}><tspan data-lang-en>{s.en[0]}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{s.vi[0]}</tspan></text>
        <text x={120 + i * 220} y="108" text-anchor="middle" class={s.red ? 'vr' : 'v'}><tspan data-lang-en>{s.en[1]}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{s.vi[1]}</tspan></text>
        {i < 3 && <polygon points={`${218 + i * 220},92 ${236 + i * 220},92 ${236 + i * 220},86 ${248 + i * 220},92 ${236 + i * 220},98 ${236 + i * 220},92`} class="arrow" />}
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x="30" y="188" class="s"><tspan data-lang-en>the bug lives here</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>lỗi nằm ở đây</tspan></text>
    <line x1="30" y1="198" x2="400" y2="198" class="lnr" />
    <text x="870" y="188" text-anchor="end" class="s"><tspan data-lang-en>the blame lands here</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>nhưng bị đổ ở đây</tspan></text>
    <line x1="470" y1="198" x2="870" y2="198" class="ln" />
    <text x="30" y="250" class="s"><tspan data-lang-en>A health check is just another request, so it queues like one.</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Health check cũng chỉ là một request, nên nó cũng phải xếp hàng.</tspan></text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>From one blocking endpoint to a process the load balancer gives up on.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Từ một endpoint chặn tới một process mà load balancer bỏ cuộc.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .bep6i { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .bep6i-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .bep6i svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 700px; height: auto; }
  .bep6i text { font-size: 13.5px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .bep6i .h { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); font-size: 15px; }
  .bep6i .code { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); font-size: 14px; }
  .bep6i .s { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .bep6i .v { fill: var(--text); font-weight: 700; }
  .bep6i .vr { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .bep6i .tk { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .bep6i .axis { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .bep6i .grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .bep6i .ok { fill: var(--gold-tint-bg); stroke: var(--gold-icon); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .bep6i .bad { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .bep6i .box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .bep6i .arrow { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .bep6i .arrowr { fill: var(--red); }
  .bep6i .ln { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .bep6i .lnr { stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.8; }
  .bep6i figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
